        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Five intervals, roughly <strong class="text-white">50 to 70 minutes a year</strong> and
            about $20 of consumables. The two tasks carrying almost all the value are the
            after-session wipe and lubricating every 40 to 50 hours.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Work in running hours rather than months, clean before you lubricate, and stop
            immediately for a burning smell, sparking, smoke, or a belt that moves when the
            machine is off. The full schedule is in the
            <a href="/treadmill-maintenance/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">maintenance pillar</a>.
          </p>
